#4322: Size-weighted group metrics use another metric's sample count
  State: open, Comments: 1
  Body: ## Description

Size-weighted group aggregation uses a task's single `sample_len` for every metric, even when that task produced different numbers of values for different metrics.

This biases group scores toward tasks whose unrelated metric has the largest count. The point estimate and its pooled uncertainty are both weighted with the wrong denominator.

## How it happens

Task aggregation records each metric/filter length internally but returns only the maximum as `sample_len`. Group aggregati

